{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I have loved:</b> The sense is that the children of one father were brothers, Esau and Jacob, and I swore that I will establish My covenant with Isaac, and I loved Jacob, and I gave him the land of Canaan, which I swore to his fathers to give to their seed, and I drove Esau from the land of HaShem, and I gave him Mount Seir for the sake of the honor of his father, but on account of his wickedness I made his mountains a desolation. And so He called it a border of wickedness. And behold, you are the children of Jacob — behold, you dwell in the land of the covenant."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:05.905725356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}